## Core Entities

List the main data models. Each entity must:
- Have a UUID primary key
- Inherit from `Base` in `app.models.base`
- Use `Mapped[...]` and `mapped_column()` (SQLAlchemy 2.0 style)
- Use `default=` not `default_factory=` in `mapped_column()`
- Use naive `datetime` (no timezone) — use `utc_now()` from `app.core.utils`
- Have an alembic migration

### Example: {PRIMARY_ENTITY}
```
{PRIMARY_ENTITY}
├── id: UUID (PK)
├── name: str (required)
├── status: enum ["active", "inactive"] (default: "active")
├── created_at: datetime
└── updated_at: datetime
```

### Example: {CHILD_ENTITY}
```
{CHILD_ENTITY}
├── id: UUID (PK)
├── {primary_entity_id}: UUID (FK → {PRIMARY_ENTITY}, ondelete=CASCADE)
├── title: str (required)
├── value: float (required)
├── created_at: datetime
└── updated_at: datetime
```

## User Stories / Screens

### Screen 1: Dashboard
- Summary cards: key metrics at a glance
- Recent activity or alerts feed
- Top action items surfaced by AI
- Quick action buttons (add record, trigger scan, etc.)

### Screen 2: {PRIMARY_ENTITY} List
- Table view with pagination, search, filters
- Status filter and bulk actions (delete, export)
- "Add New" modal/form

### Screen 3: {PRIMARY_ENTITY} Detail
- Record info card with edit/delete
- Related {CHILD_ENTITY} list
- Activity timeline
- Add {CHILD_ENTITY} button

### Screen 4: {CHILD_ENTITY} List / Explorer
- Filterable table or board view
- Search, sort, export
- Status transitions (e.g., open → resolved)

### Screen 5: AI Copilot (REQUIRED — P0 Mandate)
- Floating chat widget on every page (bottom-right)
- Full-page `/copilot` route with conversation history
- Context-aware: knows the current domain data
- Suggests next actions proactively
- Falls back to local Ollama when cloud LLM unavailable

